      "writtenOn": "2017-04-22T00:37:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, they\u0027re optional and depend on the chip variant. Please notice CONFIG_NPCX_PSL_MODE is used to declare npcx7 ec support this hardware feature. If the developers want to use PSL circuit for hibernating, they need to add CONFIG_HIBERNATE_PSL in the board-level driver. (CONFIG_HIBERNATE_PSL will be introduced in the npcx7 system driver.)\n\nRegarding undefined items, these three definitions are only related to CHIP_VARIANT and cannot be modified in the board-level driver. Should we need to add undefined items in \"include/config.h\"? Or change prefix CONFIG_ to the other?",
